    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s739-metadata",
      "source": "sections/s739-metadata.md",
      "source_hash": "c6b0e9de8d53bbf5e507d5469cb2214bf9a6ec39b6331e0dac7a0b1f374bb71a",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Adding file metadata in the upload section works as for the submission form, with the path /sections/<form-name>/files/<file-index>/metadata/<metadata>: append with /-, insert at a zero-based index, or add an array at the field path to initialise or replace all its values. The example sets the first uploaded file's dc.title to MyFile.pdf. More examples are on the submission-form section page.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s740-access-condition",
      "source": "sections/s740-access-condition.md",
      "source_hash": "9c0ed943240db0276d7d109310614f3a98d98a0a94c098ce477ba7640dc528ab",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Adding a file access condition: a PATCH add on /sections/<form-name>/files/<file-index>/accessConditions/- appends one, and an add of an array on the file's access conditions path replaces them all. The attributes needed depend on the condition's name, as configured in submissionuploads: openaccess needs nothing more, while embargo is rejected without a startDate. The array is never null, so clients can always append rather than add at an index.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
    },
