    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s752-multipart-post-method",
      "source": "sections/s752-multipart-post-method.md",
      "source_hash": "5cf095eeb34f14d8f1efbe5366c0453d1e218cf58bc01ee677c48cc39299b886",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A multipart POST to /api/submission/workspaceitems creates a workspace item in one of two ways. From a remote resource: a text/uri-list body naming an external entry value (for example an ORCID record), whose metadata is imported straight away with no preview, since the user has already chosen the record and the item starts empty. From files: one or more uploaded files, where files with no parser are discarded, the first parseable file pre-fills the metadata and the others are just attached, and a file holding more than one entry gives 422. curl examples are given for both.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s753-single-workspace-item",
      "source": "sections/s753-single-workspace-item.md",
      "source_hash": "176d01e34c4aff9429f10ae2dab2af27c93a051b295e4eb3f25fb2b7764b38e8",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "/api/submission/workspaceitems/<id> returns one workspace item. The in-progress submission's data sit in a sections map that follows the submission definition and is open for extension (each section type has its own JSON structure; the example shows collection, identifiers, form pages, license, cclicense and uploads). It links to collection (where the item will be created), item (which holds the data), submissionDefinition and supervisionOrders.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s754-multipart-post-method-on-a-single-workspaceitem",
      "source": "sections/s754-multipart-post-method-on-a-single-workspaceitem.md",
      "source_hash": "68144012bdb9b3acf35aa540a6a6b31d8880a102d622879c7712db53cd00dfb3",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A multipart POST to a single workspace item usually adds a new file to the section named by the upload variable (uploads by default), handled by that section's implementation, and returns 201 with the workspace item's new state. An owning collection may be given; if omitted, the first collection the user can submit to is used.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt8n45nmwCHCTpc28EY"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s755-linked-entities",
